@title Telemetry Pipeline
@subtitle Turbine telemetry for 6 offshore wind farms, eu-north-1
@author Asset Data team, Owner
@date Reviewed 2026-10-02

kpi Peak load | 18,000 msg/s | 24 shards | neutral
kpi Uplink buffer | 6 hours | then oldest dropped | bad
kpi Wind farms | 6 | one edge gateway each | neutral

# Overview
Turbine readings flow from each farm into one central stream and are processed once. The processed data then splits into a fast store for dashboards and a cheap archive for audits.

# Pipeline diagram
diagram pipe dir=TB title="Telemetry pipeline, farm to dashboard"
pipe: ctrl "Turbine Controllers" svc
pipe: gw "Edge Gateway" svc "buffers 6 h on disk" focus
pipe: stream "Telemetry Stream" queue "24 shards"
pipe: proc "Stream Processor" fn focus
pipe: tsdb "Timeseries Store" db
pipe: archive "Raw Archive" store
pipe: alert "Alerting Service" svc
pipe: dash "Operations Dashboard" user
pipe: ctrl -> gw : OPC UA, 1 Hz
pipe: gw -> stream : MQTT over TLS, 5 s batches
pipe: stream -> proc : consumer
pipe: proc -> tsdb : 10 s aggregates
pipe: proc -> archive : Parquet every 15 min
pipe: proc -> alert : threshold breach
pipe: tsdb -> dash : queries
pipe: group site "On site at each farm (outside cloud account)" ctrl, gw
pipe: group cloud "Cloud account, eu-north-1" stream, proc, tsdb, archive, alert, dash

The Edge Gateway sends readings to the Telemetry Stream over MQTT over TLS, batched every 5 seconds. The Stream Processor writes Parquet files to the Raw Archive every 15 minutes.

# Capacity and retention
table = Component,Size,Retention; **Telemetry Stream**,"24 shards, 18,000 messages/s at peak",—; **Timeseries Store**,—,"7 days in memory, 3 years on magnetic storage"; **Raw Archive**,—,"10 years, moved to cold storage after 90 days"

# If the uplink fails
!! The Edge Gateway buffers at most **6 hours** of readings on disk. If the uplink is down longer than that, the oldest readings are dropped and cannot be recovered.

1. The Edge Gateway keeps collecting readings from the Turbine Controllers and writes them to its local disk buffer.
2. When the link returns, it replays the buffered readings to the Telemetry Stream in order.
3. Past 6 hours of outage, the gateway drops the oldest readings first to make room for new ones.
